    "created_at": "2023-04-02T19:58:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-02T19:58:17Z",
    "body": "Deno would be in favor of landing this. Allowing only `ws:` and `wss:` protocols is a constant source of pain for web devs. [A very simple query on GitHub Code Search](https://github.com/search?type=code&auto_enroll=true&q=%22scheme%20%3D%20%27wss%22%20OR%20%22protocol%20%3D%20%27wss%22%20OR%20%22scheme%20%3D%20%5C%22wss%22%20OR%20%22protocol%20%3D%20%5C%22wss%22) reveals at least 9k candidate files in open source that have `if (protocol == \"https:\") scheme = \"wss:\"`.\r\n\r\nFolks, please let's ship this. It's trivial, it has tests, and it's going to make everyone's lives just slightly less terrible.\r\n\r\nSo, I'll ask for positions from WebKit and Mozilla here again: @annevk, @saschanaz, thoughts?",
